.TH "PB-CONFIG-REPOSITORY-CREDENTIALS-REMOVE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-repository-credentials-remove - Remove this machine's saved repository credentials


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config repository credentials remove <repository> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove this machine's saved repository credentials

.PP
Resolve a custom Git repository by ID or name and remove this machine's saved authentication profile. The repository registration and its content remain available; configure another profile before operations that require private repository authentication.

.PP
Configuration commands distinguish local CLI settings from synchronized repository content. Inspect current state before changing it; synchronization reports conflicts instead of silently overwriting one side. The --json option provides structured output for scripts where supported.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for remove

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-repository-credentials(1)\fP
